From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:26:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-gpu-virgl: refuse to scan out a resource with no
 texture

A guest names a resource it created in SET_SCANOUT, and the device
hands the resource's GL texture to the display. One with no GL object
behind it, such as a resource that lives only in guest memory, has a
texture of 0: the D-Bus display aborted the machine on it, and the other
displays had nothing to show.

Refuse it as an invalid resource, as one that does not exist is.

Signed-off-by: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
index 9bda572426..658df247d5 100644
--- a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
+++ b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-virgl.c
@@ -581,6 +581,13 @@ static void virgl_cmd_set_scanout(VirtIOGPU *g,
             cmd->error = VIRTIO_GPU_RESP_ERR_INVALID_RESOURCE_ID;
             return;
         }
+        if (!info.tex_id && !d3d_tex2d) {
+            qemu_log_mask(LOG_GUEST_ERROR,
+                          "%s: resource %d has no texture to scan out\n",
+                          __func__, ss.resource_id);
+            cmd->error = VIRTIO_GPU_RESP_ERR_INVALID_RESOURCE_ID;
+            return;
+        }
         if (!virtio_gpu_check_scanout_bounds(ss.scanout_id, ss.resource_id,
                                              info.width, info.height, &ss.r,
                                              &cmd->error)) {
